    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Rowe and Miller Medical Group\nRe: Amanda Ball (DOB 07, 2024: Ms. Amanda Ball presented for a routine follow-up to her COPD and to refill her medication prescription. Her blood pressure was 135/73, and her weight was recorded at 153 pounds. Ms. Ball is currently on roflumilast 500 mcg which she has been taking consistently. Her pulmonary function tests indicate that her FEV1 is 50% of the predicted value, a finding that has remained stable over the past few visits. She reports no new symptoms, and she continues to do well with her current treatment regimen.\n\n---\n\nDecember 29, 2023: Ms. Ball visited our clinic to receive her annual influenza vaccination. Her blood pressure was 128/67, and her weight was 156 pounds. During this visit, we reviewed her ongoing COPD management. Her FEV1 remains at 50% of the predicted value. She is adhering to her roflumilast medication without issues. She continues to report no significant respiratory symptoms aside from occasional minor complaints of dry mouth.\n\n---\n\nJuly 20, 2023: On July 20, 2023, Ms. Ball came in for a review of her lab results and to discuss her COPD management. Her blood pressure was 134/63, and she weighed 150 pounds. She is on roflumilast 500 mcg daily and her pulmonary function tests indicate an FEV1 of 50% of the predicted value. She is tolerating her medication well and has not reported any new symptoms. Her condition remains stable.\n\n---\n\nFebruary 09, 2023: Ball was seen on February 9, 2023, for a follow-up regarding her COPD. Her blood pressure was 128/65, and she weighed 144 pounds. Her FEV1 was measured at 50% of the predicted value. She is on 500 mcg, which she takes regularly. She has been experiencing mild, manageable symptoms consistent with her known COPD diagnosis.\n\n---\n\nAugust 31, 2022: Ms. Ball's visit August 31, 2022, was for a COPD follow-up. Her blood pressure was 128/73, and she weighed 156 pounds. Her FEV1 was recorded at 50% of the predicted value. She continues to take roflumilast 500 mcg, and there have been no new developments in her condition. She reports she is managing her symptoms well with her current treatment.\n\n---\n\nMarch 23, 2022: On March 23, 2022, Ms. Ball came in for a routine COPD follow-up. Her blood pressure was 130/70, and she weighed 153 pounds. Her FEV1 remains at 50% of the predicted value. She is taking roflumilast 500 mcg and reports no significant changes in her respiratory status. She continues to do well.\n\n---\n\nOctober 12, 2021: Ms. Ball was seen\n"
